#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
HPA: It automatically increases or decreases the number of pod replicas, based on resource usage or other metrics

VPA (Vertical Pod Autoscaler): It automatically adjusts the CPU and memory requests and limits of Pods based on their resource usage.
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
Step 1 — Install Metrics Server
Reference: https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server

kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/metrics-server/releases/latest/download/components.
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
Step 2 — Edit the Metrics Server Deployment

To Open the deployment for editing:
-----------------------------------
kubectl edit deployment -n kube-system metrics-server

Add the following argument under spec.containers[].args:
--------------------------------------------------------
args:
  - --kubelet-insecure-tls

Example snippet in context:
---------------------------
spec:
  containers:
    - name: metrics-server
      args:
        - --cert-dir=/tmp
        - --secure-port=4443
        - --kubelet-insecure-tls        # <-- add this line
        - --kubelet-preferred-address-types=InternalIP,ExternalIP,Hostname
#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------#